lavapipe on Kosmos (docs/gpu3d.md G2). What it reaches for that a Kosmos
process does not have, each left out rather than imitated:

- gallivm's disassembler writes into a std::ostringstream, and Kosmos's
  libc++ has no locale streams; it writes into LLVM's raw_string_ostream,
  as LLVM's own patches do (runtime/patches/llvm/).
- gallivm's LLJIT would search the process for symbols, which needs
  dlopen, and set up a platform's runtime; as llvmtest's does (G1), it is
  told there is no process to search and no platform, so what a shader
  calls is what gallivm defines to it.
- gallivm's ORC JIT reaches its compiler with dynamic_cast, and LLVM is
  built without RTTI here; the compiler is a SimpleCompiler by
  construction - gallivm made it - so a static_cast says the same.
- drm.h, which lavapipe includes for DRM's format codes alone, includes
  the BSDs' ioctl header; there is no ioctl on Kosmos (CLAUDE.md), and
  the codes need none.
- the Vulkan runtime includes dlfcn.h for RenderDoc, which is off; it is
  included only when RenderDoc is on.
- translate's x86 path assembles code into memory it maps writable and
  executable at once, and Nebula never maps a page both; on Kosmos it is
  not taken, and the generic path - or LLVM's, which writes then flips -
  does the work.
- the drivers' configuration matches a program's name against a regular
  expression, and Kosmos's libc has no regex.h; it is built with
  NO_REGEX, as on Windows without one, and such an option never matches.

